        "d6": CheckGuide(proves: "Errors are stored in the database for the export.",
                         steps: ["Run all automatic, or: Crash catcher → Write a test entry."], place: .noScooter),
        "u1": CheckGuide(proves: "Running checks show how far along they are, and multi-step checks tick their own steps (so you never have to guess).",
                         steps: ["Developer → Checks → tap Run all automatic: a bar and \"Step N of 8\" appear.",
                                 "While it runs, find d1 and d7 (All checks): a bar with the percentage shows on the one that is running.",
                                 "Look at b9, c5, c6 and c7: each has a Steps list (\"0 of 5\" …) with empty circles.",
                                 "With the scooter: start b8 (Scooter → Start 4-min test): a bar with \"3:20 left\" counts down.",
                                 "Tap Pass if the bars move and the steps tick as you do them, Fail if not (add a Note)."], place: .noScooter),
        "u2": CheckGuide(proves: "This build is 0.6 and carries the decided thresholds: speed warning on above 45 km/h and off below 43 (T99), safety margin +10% on decisions (T101).",
                         steps: ["Nothing to do: it marks itself when the app opens.", "Look at Settings → About for the version line (v1 · 0.6)."], place: .noScooter),
        "u3": CheckGuide(proves: "The fake scooter can also replay the phone's own GPS and barometer from a real ride, on the same clock as the scooter data. Later steps use this to test the ride engine without riding.",
                         steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (it runs this check in a second).", "Or just open the app: nothing else to do.",
                                 "Result: how many GPS fixes and barometer readings replayed and how close the phone track is to the scooter log."], place: .noScooter),
        "u4": CheckGuide(proves: "Rides can be stored and removed: the ride, its samples, raw data, gaps and stops. Tests like this run in a temporary database, so your real rides are never touched.",
                         steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (it runs this check in a second).",
                                 "Result: what was written, read back and deleted, and your real ride count before and after (it must be the same)."], place: .noScooter),
        "u8": CheckGuide(proves: "The Rides list rules work: the newest ride sits under Latest, the others are grouped by day, short hops (0.5 to 2 km) are kept apart, discarded pieces are hidden, the date filter (Today, This week, This month, All time) picks the right rides and a deleted ride disappears.",
                         steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (it runs this check in a second).",
                                 "Result: one note per rule. Made-up rides in a temporary database are used, your real rides are never touched.",
                                 "Then open the Rides tab: empty now, with the filter menu top right (v1 label bottom right)."], place: .noScooter),
        "u9": CheckGuide(proves: "The ride engine starts a ride the right way: a ride begins when the wheel turns faster than 2 km/h and is confirmed by the motor current, the GPS speed or 50 m of GPS movement. Walking the scooter, spinning the wheel on the stand and a kick-start (the three autostart traps) are handled: walking is cancelled or trimmed away, a spin is cancelled within 20 s, a kick-start is kept. Start ride skips the confirm step and Not riding removes the ride without a trace.",
                         steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (it runs this check in a second, on the fake scooter).",
                                 "Result: one tick per rule, with the seconds a spin took to cancel and the signal that confirmed the kick-start.",
                                 "The real-scooter versions (t1 walk, t2 spin, t3 kick) come with the Trap test in the M1 check list."], place: .noScooter),
        "u10": CheckGuide(proves: "The ride engine ends rides the right way and keeps the ride's stops: the scooter switching itself off ends the ride at once; a scooter that drops while you stand still ends it after 30 seconds; the auto-off after 5 minutes standing and 10 minutes of standstill end it too; the end time is always the last movement. Pushing the scooter (walking pace, no motor power, 30 s) is a walking stretch: its distance counts, but not in the average speed, and when the battery ran out the % is kept for the range. Switching off at a light and riding on within 10 minutes offers \"Same ride?\". If the app is killed mid-ride it carries on, or after more than 2 minutes the ride is closed as recovered.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (it runs this check in a few seconds, on the fake scooter).",
                                  "Result: one tick per rule, with the seconds and kilometres it found.",
                                  "The real versions (e2 scooter off, e3 Same ride, a real push of ~100 m) come with the M1 check list."], place: .noScooter),
        "u11": CheckGuide(proves: "When the scooter link drops mid-ride the phone takes over, but only after about 5 seconds, so a 1-second drop (seen 4 times on build 27) changes nothing. Then the speed comes from GPS (smoothed over 3 s, labelled \"GPS\"), the battery shows \"~N% est.\", and the stretch is kept as a gap; on reconnect the scooter numbers come back and the odometer fills in the distance. Ride totals stay scooter-only. The speed warning turns red with SLOW above 45 km/h and clears below 43, on the scooter's speed and on GPS speed while disconnected, without flickering.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (it runs this check in a second, on the fake scooter).",
                                  "Result: one tick per rule, with the seconds the warning switched on and off and the metres the odometer filled in.",
                                  "The real versions (p3 walk out of range and back, w4 speed warning on real rides) come with the M1 check list."], place: .noScooter),
        "u16": CheckGuide(proves: "The backup files are real and readable: a full backup (a compressed copy of the whole database) and a small file per ride are written, read back and compared, latest.json holds the settings, and old full backups are removed so only the newest three stay. Nothing touches your real backup folder or rides.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (a second or two, in a temporary folder).",
                                  "Result: one tick per part.",
                                  "The real folder: Developer → Backup folder (d2), then finish a ride (d10)."], place: .noScooter),
        "q1": CheckGuide(proves: "Recording a ride does not drain the phone: at most 10% of its battery per 30 minutes of riding.",
                         steps: ["Ride 15 minutes or more with the phone not charging (the Recorder notes the phone battery at the start and at the end).",
                                 "Result: the % used per ride and per 30 minutes. Not judged when the phone was charging or the ride was shorter."], place: .ride),
        "d10": CheckGuide(proves: "After a real ride the app writes its backup to your folder: a ride file in CorckieApp Backup/rides, plus a full backup when the last one is a week old.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Backup folder → Pick folder (check d2 first).",
                                  "Finish a ride.",
                                  "Result: ✅ with the file name; Settings → Last backup shows the time. Open the folder in Files to see it."], place: .ride),
        "u15": CheckGuide(proves: "The ride summary (shown when a ride ends, and when you tap a ride in Rides) is built right from what was stored: time, moving time, distance, average speed, battery start to end, top speed, energy, stops, elevation and temperature, with a map path coloured by speed (dashed where the phone recorded alone, grey where you walked) and plain notes for a recovered ride, missing scooter or GPS readings and a hot scooter. No records, badges or comparisons. A ride without GPS shows a No GPS card instead of the map.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (runs in a second, on a made-up ride in a temporary database).",
                                  "Result: one tick per part.",
                                  "To look at the real screen: Rides → tap a ride (a ride you did, or a simulated one once M1-15 is in)."], place: .noScooter),
        "u14": CheckGuide(proves: "The live ride screen shows the right things and stays safe: the Ready view (opened from the Going for a ride? notification) shows the map, battery and speed 0 with no clock and no stop button, and is the only live view that can be closed; once a ride is on there is no close button, no tab bar and no swipe-down, and only holding the stop button for a full second ends the ride (a tap does nothing). The speed turns red with SLOW above 45 km/h and clears below 43; GPS speed is greyed and labelled GPS with the battery shown as ~N% est.; banners come one at a time and cannot be tapped from 5 km/h; No GPS shows after 10 seconds.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (runs in a second, on made-up readings).",
                                  "Result: one tick per rule.",
                                  "The real screens: Developer → Simulated scooter (arrives with M1-15), and a real ride (l3, f2, f3 in the M1 check list)."], place: .noScooter),
        "u13": CheckGuide(proves: "Home shows the right thing in every state: first use and a scooter that is not connected show the amber Connect your scooter (never Start ride, because no ride can start before the connection is confirmed); a connected scooter shows its battery and Start ride; a connect that has not worked after 30 seconds says Can't find the scooter · Is it switched on? with Try again; a ride in progress says so.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (runs in a second).",
                                  "Result: one tick per state.",
                                  "Then open Home: with the scooter off it shows Scooter not connected and when you last saw it; switch the scooter on and Start ride appears."], place: .noScooter),
        "o1": CheckGuide(proves: "Onboarding takes three presses: Connect (the scooter that was found), Allow (location Always and motion, iOS asks) and Allow or Not now (notifications with sound). Then you are on Home. No tour.",
                         steps: ["Developer → Show onboarding (your scooter stays paired).",
                                 "Press Connect, then Allow (answer the iOS prompts), then Allow or Not now.",
                                 "The check turns green with the number of presses. Run all automatic marks the rules too."], place: .noScooter),
        "u12": CheckGuide(proves: "The Recorder works end to end: the fake scooter plays rides 1 and 2 into the same Recorder that records your real rides (ride engine, a sample every 5 seconds, the raw scooter packets, stops, the ride row), into a temporary database, and the stored ride gives the measured totals: about 437 Wh and 16.3 km, 322 Wh and 13.7 km. Then the app is \"killed\" mid-ride and opened again 10 minutes later: the ride is closed as recovered at its last sample. Your real rides are never touched.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic (this step takes about 10 seconds).",
